  "description": "You're Epic Games, and your fort-building game was locked behind a price until you made a free battle royale mode.\n\nSources:\n- Wikipedia: Fortnite Battle Royale: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortnite_Battle_Royale\n- Wikipedia: Fortnite: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortnite\n- Wikipedia: Epic Games: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epic_Games\n\nFrom the cited pages: Fortnite began from an Epic game jam around 2011; early access started July 25, 2017; Save the World passed one million players by August 2017; PUBG sold over 5 million copies three months after its March 2017 release; Battle Royale was built in about two months and released free on September 26, 2017; over 10 million players in two weeks; over 125 million players by June 2018; SuperData reported $2.4 billion earned in 2018; V-Bucks buy cosmetics such as skins and emotes. Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #fortnite #epicgames #howtheymakemoney",
